---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Beige Box Terms and Conditions"
      description="Terms and Conditions for Beige Box, an iOS app of original pretend vintage computers with a one-time unlock."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main id="main">
      <article class="policy tile">
        <p class="tile-kicker">Beige Box</p>
        <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
        <p class="date"><strong>Last updated:</strong> November 1, 2026</p>

        <p>
          Beige Box is an iOS app with three original pretend computers from earlier eras. By using
          the app, you agree to use it lawfully and in accordance with these terms and Apple's
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>What the app includes</h2>
        <p>
          The app includes three computers: HOMEROOM 82, BEIGE BOX and candy 99. Each comes with
          programs to browse the web, write, draw, program in BASIC, play Worm, manage your files,
          and visit the BeigeNet bulletin board. The computers, their names, sounds and artwork are
          original designs. They are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or copies of any real computer
          or computer maker.
        </p>

        <h2>The one-time unlock</h2>
        <p>
          Beige Box is free to download and lets you pick a computer. Using the computers requires a
          single non-consumable in-app purchase. It is not a subscription and does not renew. It
          unlocks all three computers and any computers added to the app in later updates. The unlock
          supports Apple Family Sharing.
        </p>
        <p>
          The price shown in the App Store for your region is the price that applies. Purchases are
          made through Apple, and Apple's terms govern payment, billing and refunds. Refunds are
          requested from Apple; this app cannot issue them. Nothing in these terms limits refund or
          consumer rights you have under the law where you live.
        </p>
        <p>
          Buying and restoring need an internet connection. After the unlock is confirmed on your
          device, the computers work offline, except for web browsing. If a purchase is refunded or
          revoked, paid access ends. Your files are not deleted when that happens.
        </p>

        <h2>Restoring a purchase</h2>
        <p>
          Restore on the unlock screen restores access on a device signed in to the Apple Account
          that bought the unlock, or a Family Sharing member's account. It does not restore deleted
          files, and it is not a backup.
        </p>

        <h2>Browsing the web</h2>
        <p>
          Surf shows real third-party websites, redrawn at a low resolution in the style of each
          computer. The developer does not control those websites and is not responsible for their
          content, accuracy or availability, which may include material you find offensive. Some
          sites will not work fully in this redrawn view. Use a regular browser for banking, payments,
          or anything important. Your use of each website is governed by that website's own terms.
          Searches are provided by DuckDuckGo.
        </p>

        <h2>Your files</h2>
        <p>
          Documents, programs and pictures you make are yours. This app claims no ownership of them
          and does not upload them. They are stored on your device, so they can be lost if the app is
          deleted, the device is lost, or its storage fails. Deleting a file in My Disk is immediate
          and cannot be undone. You can use Export or the Files app to keep copies; the app does not
          operate a cloud backup.
        </p>

        <h2>The BeigeNet bulletin board</h2>
        <p>
          BeigeNet is currently a local demonstration on your device, not a shared message board. Its
          welcome posts are sample messages included with the app, not posts from other people.
          Messages you post stay on your device, are not seen by anyone else, and are cleared when the
          app is fully closed.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          Do not use the app to break the law, to harass anyone, or to access or share content you
          have no right to access or share. You are responsible for what you create, type, and visit
          in the app.
        </p>

        <h2>The app and its content</h2>
        <p>
          The app, its computers, built-in programs, sounds and artwork remain the property of the
          developer. You may use them within the app. Please do not copy or republish them as your
          own product.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          Features and content may change as the app develops. The app is provided as it is, without
          a promise that it will be uninterrupted or error free. To the extent the law allows, the
          developer is not liable for lost files or for indirect losses arising from use of the app or
          of third-party websites opened in it. If these terms change, the date above will change.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent to
          <a href="mailto:randyventures06@gmail.com">randyventures06@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

